{"slug":"longest-palindromic-substring","title":"Longest Palindromic Substring","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"medium","order":168,"tags":["strings","palindrome","expand-around-center"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Grow a palindrome from its centre","body":["Every palindrome has a centre: a single letter (odd length) or the gap between two letters (even length). Starting from a centre and moving one step left and one step right as long as the two letters are equal grows the palindrome as far as it goes.",{"code":"for c in range(2 * n - 1):\n    l = c // 2\n    r = l + c % 2          # same letter for odd, next letter for even\n    while l >= 0 and r < n and s[l] == s[r]:\n        l -= 1\n        r += 1\n    # the palindrome is s[l + 1 : r], its length is r - l - 1"},"There are `2n - 1` centres and each expansion costs at most O(n), so the total is O(n^2): fine for a few thousand letters. (A cleverer linear algorithm exists, but this one is much simpler.)"]},"statement":["Given a word, find its longest substring (block of consecutive letters) that reads the same forwards and backwards. If there are several of the same length, print the one that starts first."],"inputFormat":["A single word of lowercase letters."],"outputFormat":["Print the palindrome."],"constraints":["1 <= length <= 2000"],"examples":[{"input":"babad\n","output":"bab\n","note":"Both bab and aba have length 3; bab starts first."},{"input":"cbbd\n","output":"bb\n","note":"bb is the longest."}],"hints":["A palindrome grows symmetrically from its centre.","There are two kinds of centres: a letter and the gap between two letters.","For each centre expand while the two outer letters are equal, and remember the longest one (the first one on ties)."],"starter":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Expand around each of the `2n - 1` centres. A palindrome is only replaced by a strictly longer one, so the first one of the maximum length is kept."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(1).","code":{"python":"s = input().strip()\n\nn = len(s)\nbestL, bestLen = 0, 1\nfor c in range(2 * n - 1):\n    l = c // 2\n    rr = l + c % 2\n    while l >= 0 and rr < n and s[l] == s[rr]:\n        l -= 1\n        rr += 1\n    if rr - l - 1 > bestLen:\n        bestLen = rr - l - 1\n        bestL = l + 1\nprint(s[bestL:bestL + bestLen])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    int n = s.size(), bestL = 0, bestLen = 1;\n    for (int c = 0; c < 2 * n - 1; c++) {\n        int l = c / 2, rr = l + c % 2;\n        while (l >= 0 && rr < n && s[l] == s[rr]) {\n            l--;\n            rr++;\n        }\n        if (rr - l - 1 > bestLen) {\n            bestLen = rr - l - 1;\n            bestL = l + 1;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << s.substr(bestL, bestLen) << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String s = sc.next();\n\n        int n = s.length(), bestL = 0, bestLen = 1;\n        for (int c = 0; c < 2 * n - 1; c++) {\n            int l = c / 2, rr = l + c % 2;\n            while (l >= 0 && rr < n && s.charAt(l) == s.charAt(rr)) {\n                l--;\n                rr++;\n            }\n            if (rr - l - 1 > bestLen) {\n                bestLen = rr - l - 1;\n                bestL = l + 1;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(s.substring(bestL, bestL + bestLen));\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"babad\n","output":"bab\n"},{"input":"cbbd\n","output":"bb\n"},{"input":"a\n","output":"a\n"},{"input":"ab\n","output":"a\n"},{"input":"aaaa\n","output":"aaaa\n"},{"input":"abcda\n","output":"a\n"},{"input":"baababbbbabbbbbbbbaaaabababbabaabbaaaabb\n","output":"abbbbbbbba\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"baaabbaaaabbaaaabbaaab\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"hyjyh\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"caabcbbaabbcbaac\n"}]}